{
  "rule": "mcp-server-launch",
  "why": "npm reads .npmrc with the ini parser: a quoted key is the key, and an inline comment after a value is not part of it (measured with npm 11.6.2 npm config get). Main read the file line by line with a regular expression, so a quoted registry key pointing npx at another host passed next to an allowlisted launch, while the public default registry followed by a comment made the launch unexemptable. Both sides track the same .mcp.json launch and its allowlist line. The pass side .npmrc names the default registry with an inline comment; the fail side sets the quoted registry key to another host. Without the ini reading the pass side goes red and the fail side goes green.",
